WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.192
Category standardization is more than text cleaning.

00:00:03.192 --> 00:00:09.267
If several labels should map to one canonical category, that mapping reflects business meaning.

00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:11.727
You need a documented rule.

00:00:11.727 --> 00:00:16.032
Do not merge categories simply because their names look similar.

00:00:16.032 --> 00:00:19.977
The transformation should reflect the intended taxonomy.

00:00:19.977 --> 00:00:25.752
Standardization should make equivalent values comparable without inventing facts.

00:00:25.752 --> 00:00:33.982
Lowercasing an email or normalizing a known category map is different from guessing what an ambiguous value

00:00:33.982 --> 00:00:38.720
was supposed to mean. Good cleaning reduces representation noise while preserving uncertainty.
